// The remainder of a line after its first word: past the run of spaces that
// follows it, to the end. `write`'s text and a command's argument text are
// this same cut, so it is one function rather than two that happen to agree.
sh_tail(string s, int at) {
  int sh_skip_v = sh_skip(s, at);
  int len_v = len(s);
  string ret_s = cut(s, sh_skip_v, len_v);
} return string ret_s;
("note.txt hello world", 8):("hello world")
("a.txt hi", 5):("hi")

// The pack-and-read-back half of sh_str, cut out here because sh_str already
// spent its own budget getting the length and the address named.
sh_str_tail(int[] xs, word p, int len_v) {
  sh_pack(xs, p);
  string ret_s = str_of_mem(p, len_v);
} return string ret_s;
given sh_buf_init ([72, 105], (import sh_buf), 2):("Hi")
given sh_buf_init ([79, 75], (import sh_buf), 2):("OK")
